Thessians are a cadre of beings from beyond the [[Phenomena/Firmament|firmament]] who seek to end all life in the universe. They were not born gods. They ascend in tiers, each generation further from what it was, and each narrows to a single subject that becomes its whole nature: the one [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] calls [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Gremory]] gave himself to magic and grew very good at it.

Thessians are the apex of life within the [[Geography/index|Astra]]. A Thessian exists by holding a high local information density; one that loses enough of it loses coherence and temporarily ceases to exist, which is why killing one is nigh impossible. A hundred Thessians underwent Ascension from Formless' gift, and these are the Ascended Thessians.

[[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] has tracked them a long time. It knows [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]] as Thessians under those names. It knows [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]] as the fourth-generation Thessians Gremory, Astaroth and Paimon. That the last three are Thessians is news to Sedecium, and the worst kind: they were not among the original set.

Sedecium calls the gods of a world its [[Divinity/Higher Kind|higher kinds]], one to three to a planet, and says the higher kinds once gave the Thessians their names when they ascended. That service has ended, and a Thessian that rises now takes the name the universe gives it, whatever best fits its new nature. Either way, a Thessian's name is the theme or ideal it embodies, whether a creature, a concept or an emotion.

The only way Sedecium knows to kill a Thessian is a spike of a [[Phenomena/Holy Gold|rare gold metal]], growths of which appear perhaps once in three or four worlds.
